      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{PtCl}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$ has square planar geometry. $\\mathrm{Pt}: 5 d^{9} 6 s^{1}$\n<img src=\"assets\\st0035_6b38d6ca1ca9.png\"><br>\nTwo electrons are removed from $5 d$ shell and $6 s$ shell. So, hybridisation takes place is $d s p^{2}$ i.e. square planar geometry."
  }
